diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/wait-falsy-callable-combine-3c8e1d5f7a2b9046.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/wait-falsy-callable-combine-3c8e1d5f7a2b9046.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8264bc0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/wait-falsy-callable-combine-3c8e1d5f7a2b9046.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    `wait=None`, `wait=0` and `wait=sum([])` mean "no wait" again, for both
+    `Retrying` and `AsyncRetrying`. They raised
+    ``TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not callable`` once a retry happened.
+  - |
+    Adding a plain callable to a wait strategy, as in
+    ``my_callable + wait_fixed(1)``, now builds a ``wait_combine`` that sums
+    both, instead of raising ``TypeError``.
+  - |
+    ``wait_combine`` passes the retry state to its strategies positionally, so
+    plain callables may name their parameter anything.
